{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinring/tmlanguage/master/tmlanguage.json",
  "name": "BMX",
  "scopeName": "text.bmx",
  "//": [
    "**THE TWO SCOPES A HOST INJECTS INTO ARE PART OF BMX'S PROMISE, NOT AN IMPLEMENTATION DETAIL.**",
    "",
    "BMX captures a block's head and a slot's expression OPAQUELY and hands them to the host \u2014 that",
    "is BOUNDARY.md's whole rule. Highlighting has to say the same thing, or an editor would be",
    "claiming to know what `on:click=save(line.id)` means when the format does not.",
    "So the head and the expression get their own named scopes and NOTHING inside them is coloured",
    "here:",
    "    meta.block.head.bmx           everything after a block's name",
    "    meta.slot.expression.bmx      the text between {{ and }}",
    "    meta.inline-block.head.bmx    the text between [ and ] of an inline block",
    "A host injects with `injectionSelector: \"L:meta.slot.expression.bmx\"` and colours its own",
    "expression language there. Two hosts can do it differently in the same editor and neither has to",
    "patch this file. **These three names are therefore a compatibility surface**: renaming one",
    "breaks every host's grammar, so it is a major change under VERSIONING.md, exactly like renaming",
    "an AST field.",
    "Order matters twice below. A fenced code block wins over everything, because \u00a75 says its content",
    "is never parsed \u2014 a `{{` inside one is text and colouring it as a slot would be a lie an author",
    "is never parsed \u2014 a `{{` inside one is text and colouring it as a slot would be a lie an author could not turn off. There used to be a second reason \u2014 a longer `::::` fence had to be tried before `:::` \u2014 and 0.7 deleted it along with the fence-length rule: one `:name:` rule now, whose `end` backreferences the name capture so a block stays open until ITS OWN closer."
  ],
  "patterns": [
    {
      "include": "#fenced-code"
    },
    {
      "include": "#block"
    },
    {
      "include": "#heading"
    },
    {
      "include": "#quote"
    },
    {
      "include": "#list"
    },
    {
      "include": "#inline"
    }
  ],
  "repository": {
    "fenced-code": {
      "//": "First, and its content has no patterns at all. \u00a75: nothing inside is parsed.",
      "begin": "^\\s*(`{3,}|~{3,})\\s*([A-Za-z0-9_+-]*)\\s*$",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.raw.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "fenced_code.block.language.bmx"
        }
      },
      "end": "^\\s*(\\1)\\s*$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.raw.bmx"
        }
      },
      "name": "markup.raw.block.bmx"
    },
    "head-known": {
      "//": [
        "The ONLY parts of a head BMX has an opinion about, per \u00a74a: `.class` and `#id`. Everything",
        "else stays bare inside `meta.block.head.bmx` for a host to claim \u2014 including `title=\"x\"` and",
        "`on:click=save(n)`, which look like attributes and are not the format's business."
      ],
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "(\\.)([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.class.bmx"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.class.bmx"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "(#)([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.id.bmx"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.id.bmx"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "heading": {
      "match": "^\\s*(#{1,6})[ \\t]+(.*?)[ \\t]*#*$",
      "captures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.heading.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.section.bmx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#inline"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "markup.heading.bmx"
    },
    "quote": {
      "match": "^\\s*(>)[ \\t]?(.*)$",
      "captures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.quote.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "markup.quote.bmx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#inline"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "list": {
      "match": "^\\s*([-*+]|[0-9]{1,9}[.)])[ \\t]+(.*)$",
      "captures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.list.begin.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#inline"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "inline": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#escape"
        },
        {
          "include": "#code-span"
        },
        {
          "include": "#slot"
        },
        {
          "include": "#inline-block"
        },
        {
          "include": "#strong"
        },
        {
          "include": "#emphasis"
        },
        {
          "include": "#link"
        }
      ]
    },
    "escape": {
      "//": "\u00a73: only these five may be escaped, so only these are coloured as an escape.",
      "match": "\\\\[`*\\[{\\\\]",
      "name": "constant.character.escape.bmx"
    },
    "code-span": {
      "//": "Before slots: a `{{ x }}` inside backticks is text, and colouring it would be a lie.",
      "begin": "(`+)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.raw.bmx"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\1)",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.raw.bmx"
        }
      },
      "name": "markup.inline.raw.bmx"
    },
    "slot": {
      "//": [
        "**The injection point.** The expression is not coloured here, on purpose: BMX does not know",
        "what a host's expression language is. A host injects into",
        "`meta.slot.expression.bmx` and gets its own colours with no change to this file."
      ],
      "begin": "(\\{\\{)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.bmx"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\}\\})|$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.bmx"
        }
      },
      "name": "meta.slot.bmx",
      "contentName": "meta.slot.expression.bmx"
    },
    "inline-block": {
      "//": [
        "`::key[Ctrl+S]::`. Deliberately coloured differently from a slot, because the guarantee",
        "differs: a slot's value is always escaped, an inline block is a call to something the host",
        "declared. An author should be able to tell at a glance which one can produce markup."
      ],
      "begin": "(::)([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)(\\[)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.inline-block.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.function.inline-block.bmx"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.bmx"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\])(::)|$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.inline-block.bmx"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.inline-block.head.bmx"
    },
    "strong": {
      "begin": "(\\*\\*)(?=\\S)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.bold.bmx"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\*\\*)|$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.bold.bmx"
        }
      },
      "name": "markup.bold.bmx",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#escape"
        },
        {
          "include": "#code-span"
        },
        {
          "include": "#slot"
        },
        {
          "include": "#link"
        }
      ]
    },
    "emphasis": {
      "begin": "(\\*)(?=\\S)(?!\\*)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.italic.bmx"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\*)|$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.italic.bmx"
        }
      },
      "name": "markup.italic.bmx",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#escape"
        },
        {
          "include": "#code-span"
        },
        {
          "include": "#slot"
        },
        {
          "include": "#link"
        }
      ]
    },
    "link": {
      "match": "(\\[)([^\\]]*)(\\])(\\()([^)]*)(\\))",
      "captures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.link.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "string.other.link.title.bmx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#slot"
            }
          ]
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.link.bmx"
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.link.bmx"
        },
        "5": {
          "name": "markup.underline.link.bmx"
        },
        "6": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.link.bmx"
        }
      }
    },
    "block": {
      "//": "`:name: head` \u2026 `:!name:`, and `:name: -> [head] body` since 0.9. The end pattern backreferences the name capture, so a block stays open until ITS OWN closer. **The head keeps `meta.block.head.bmx` in both forms** \u2014 that scope is the compatibility surface hosts inject into, so a delimited head must not land somewhere else or every host's grammar silently stops colouring.",
      "begin": "^\\s*(:)([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)(:)(?:[ \\t]*(->)[ \\t]*(\\[)([^\\]]*)(\\])[ \\t]*(.*)|[ \\t]*(.*))$",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.block.begin.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.block.bmx"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.block.begin.bmx"
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.head.arrow.bmx"
        },
        "5": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.head.begin.bmx"
        },
        "6": {
          "name": "meta.block.head.bmx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#head-known"
            }
          ]
        },
        "7": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.head.end.bmx"
        },
        "8": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#inline"
            }
          ]
        },
        "9": {
          "name": "meta.block.head.bmx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#head-known"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "end": "^\\s*(:!)(\\2)(:)\\s*$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.block.end.bmx"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.tag.block.bmx"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.block.end.bmx"
        }
      },
      "name": "meta.block.bmx",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "$self"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
